==Galician==

===Etymology===
From Old Galician and {{inh|gl|roa-opt|novo}}, from {{inh|gl|la|novus}}, from {{inh|gl|ine-pro|*néwos}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|gl|[ˈnɔ.βʊ]|[ˈno.βʊ]}}

===Noun===
{{gl-noun|m}}

# {{lb|gl|usually|in the plural}} the [[young]] people
#: {{uxi|gl|Algúns vellos pensan que '''os novos''' só queren estar de troula|Some old people think that '''youngsters''' just want to have fun}}

===Adjective===
{{gl-adj|f=nova}}

# [[new]]
# [[young]]
# [[freshly]] [[made]]
# [[brand new]]
# [[good as new]]
# belonging to the last [[harvest]]
#* '''1301''', X. Ferro Couselo (ed.), ''A vida e a fala dos devanceiros. Escolma de documentos en galego dos séculos XIII ao XVI''. Vigo: Galaxia, page 52:
#*: ''A Eluira, I moyo de pan do ''nouo'', de qual ouueren, e I bacoro''
#*:: To Elvira, one modius of grain of the '''new''' [harvest], whatever species they happen to have there, and one piglet

